    {
      "type": "teach",
      "title": "These two never compete",
      "body": "You may be waiting to learn when to pick 𐑘 and when to pick 𐑙. You never have to. They sit next to each other on the chart, but they live at opposite ends of a word: 𐑘 only ever *starts* a syllable — yes, young, yet — and 𐑙 only ever *ends* one — sing, long, king. No English word begins with the ng sound, and none ends with the y sound. Where the letter falls tells you which one it is."
    },
